-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- M's eigenvalues exactly, and √V by its spectral projectors
-- S's characteristic polynomial is λ^z Π(λ² + μ_i); M = −S² has eigenvalues μ_i, and 0 when z > 0. With q(x) = r(−x)
-- for p(λ) = λ^a r(λ²) (as `m-from-s`), the nonzero eigenvalues are the nonzero roots of q. Where q stripped of its
-- factors x has degree at most 2 they are exact by the quadratic formula, the discriminant's root found among the
-- integers below the fuel; `eig-annihilates` checks that the eigenvalues found are all of M's on the vectors used.
sqrt-search : Nat → Nat → SQ → List SQ
sqrt-search k f d = case f of
  zero → nil
  suc g → (if sq-eq (sq-mul (sq-nat k) (sq-nat k)) d then cons (sq-nat k) nil else sqrt-search (suc k) g d)
